#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res. 2006;34:D158-D162.
#=GF CC   The members of this family belong to the H/ACA class of snoRNAs that guide
#=GF CC   the sites of modification of uridines to pseudouridines [1]. Human ACA42
#=GF CC   (SNORA42) was cloned from HeLa cells by immunoprecipitation with anti-GAR1
#=GF CC   antibody [1]. Its is predicted to guide the pseudouridylation of residues
#=GF CC   U109 and U572 of 18S rRNA [3]. ACA42 shares the same host gene with ACA26,
#=GF CC   ACA46, ACA50 [1]. This family also includes mammalian snoRNA ACA67
#=GF CC   (SNORA80) which was identified by computational screening and its
#=GF CC   expression in mouse experimentally verified by Northern blot and primer
#=GF CC   extension analysis [2]. ACA67 is proposed to guide the pseudouridylation
#=GF CC   of the same 18S rRNA residues as ACA42 [3].
#=GF WK   Small_nucleolar_RNA_SNORA42
#=GF SQ   21

